<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Boot-time run-directory job for the Q-Periapt policy agent on macOS.

  This is the launchd counterpart of q-periapt-agent.tmpfiles.conf. launchd
  creates the agent's SockPathName node itself but never the directory
  containing it, and that directory's 0710 mode is the daemon's only enforced
  admission boundary: a directory at a default mode, or one that something
  other than root put at the path, is the dangerous outcome, because the
  daemon starts normally and cannot tell the boundary is gone. The directory
  is /opt/qperiapt/run/qperiapt-agent rather than anything under
  /private/var/run, which on macOS is root:daemon 0775 with no sticky bit: a
  gid-1 process can rename or replace an entry there at will, and launchd
  would bind the socket inside whatever it substituted. This job runs
  qperiapt-agent-rundir.sh as root at boot; the script verifies with stat
  that every ancestor of the directory, from / down, is a real directory
  owned by root that group and other cannot write, creates the directory the
  first time or adopts it after, verifies that it is a real directory owned
  by the daemon account with the transport group at exactly 0710, and only
  then bootstraps the agent. Anything else is a refusal that leaves the agent
  unloaded.

  Install this file, and only this file, in /Library/LaunchDaemons:
    sudo install -d -o root -g wheel -m 0755 /opt/qperiapt/libexec \
      /opt/qperiapt/launchd /opt/qperiapt/run
    sudo install -o root -g wheel -m 0644 qperiapt-agent-rundir.sh \
      /opt/qperiapt/libexec/qperiapt-agent-rundir.sh
    sudo install -o root -g wheel -m 0644 com.qperiapt.policy-agent.plist \
      /opt/qperiapt/launchd/com.qperiapt.policy-agent.plist
    sudo install -o root -g wheel -m 0644 com.qperiapt.policy-agent-rundir.plist \
      /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.qperiapt.policy-agent-rundir.plist
    sudo launchctl bootstrap system \
      /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.qperiapt.policy-agent-rundir.plist

  The agent plist deliberately stays out of /Library/LaunchDaemons. launchd
  loads everything there at boot with no ordering among RunAtLoad jobs, so the
  agent could be loaded, and its socket bound or fail to be, before this job
  has run. The script is the only thing that loads it, and only after
  verification; the script refuses an agent plist under /Library/LaunchDaemons
  and refuses to bootstrap an agent that is already loaded.

  Conventions shared with the agent plist:
    * The socket directory sits under /opt/qperiapt, where the installer
      already has to keep everything root-owned and writable by nobody else,
      because whatever sits at the script path runs as root at every boot.
      The state paths in the agent plist stay canonical under /private/var:
      /var is a symlink to private/var, and the daemon opens each component
      O_NOFOLLOW.
    * /opt persists across boots. After the first run the job finds the
      directory it created and verifies it again rather than recreating it;
      the script never removes a directory it did not create in the same run.
    * This job runs as root (no UserName): chown to the daemon account and
      launchctl bootstrap system both require it. The script's owner and group
      parameters are NAMES, which chown resolves; the agent plist's
      SockPathOwner and SockPathGroup are NUMBERS. Template both from the same
      account and group, or the socket and its directory disagree on who may
      reach it.
    * The script runs through /bin/sh, so it needs no execute bit.
    * RunAtLoad with KeepAlive false: one run per boot, no restart on failure. A
      failed run leaves the agent unloaded -- fail closed -- and says why in the
      log file below and in the unified log under the qperiapt-agent-rundir tag.
      Re-run it by hand with:
        sudo launchctl kickstart system/com.qperiapt.policy-agent-rundir
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.qperiapt.policy-agent-rundir</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>/opt/qperiapt/libexec/qperiapt-agent-rundir.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/private/var/log/qperiapt-agent-rundir.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/private/var/log/qperiapt-agent-rundir.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
